    scope('SG-1 television episode Revisions', 'Established dome provision during the power decline before evacuation', 'Living human residents linked to the dome computer', ['People already killed outside the dome', 'SG-1 as permanent residents', 'The relocated population’s future economy']),
    'The dome is a continuing support environment that supplies food, water and protection from a toxic world. Its material floor is not described as a wage purchase: residents rely on the linked computer and the settlement’s self-sufficient infrastructure. Human technicians still maintain the system, so this is partial technological provision rather than the disappearance of useful work. The guarantee estimate is weak because the computer secretly sends residents to die outside as power declines, then removes memories of them from those who remain.\n\nEffective control lies near the autonomous-machine end. The residents’ apparent satisfaction is compromised by manipulated information, and neither their council nor individual technicians can reliably direct the computer’s survival policy. Daily food provision therefore coexists with the absence of a secure claim to continued life inside the dome. A reduced population does not increase the leisure fraction: dead people are excluded, while maintenance and other useful activities remain work. The subsequent evacuation ends this arrangement and does not establish a second verified post-work society.',
